{"slug":"/students/subjects/physics/electricity/","source":"students/subjects/physics/electricity/index.html","area":"students","kind":"division","title":"Electricity, Circuits & Electronics | Physics","description":"","subject":"physics","body":"<div class=\"max-w-6xl mx-auto\">\n    <nav class=\"mb-8\">\n      <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700\">← Back to Physics</a>\n    </nav>\n\n    <div class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-8\">\n      <header class=\"mb-12\">\n        <h1 class=\"text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Electricity, Circuits &amp; Electronics</h1>\n        <p class=\"text-lg text-gray-600\">Electrostatics, circuits, AC/DC basics, semiconductors and introductory electronics.</p>\n      </header>\n\n      <div class=\"grid gap-8\">\n        <section>         \n           <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Core Topics</h2>\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\">\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/electricity/intro-to-electricity/\" class=\"block p-6 bg-white/50 rounded-lg hover:bg-white/60 transition duration-150\">\n              <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Electric Charges &amp; Electrostatics</h3>\n              <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Coulomb's law, electric field and potential concepts.</p>\n            </a>\n          <h3 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Core Topics</h3>\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\">\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/electricity/electrostatics/\" class=\"block p-6 bg-white/50 rounded-lg hover:bg-white/60 transition duration-150\">\n              <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Electric Charges &amp; Electrostatics</h3>\n              <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Coulomb's law, electric field and potential concepts.</p>\n            </a>\n\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/electricity/circuits/\" class=\"block p-6 bg-white/50 rounded-lg hover:bg-white/60 transition duration-150\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Current Electricity</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Ohm's law, series &amp; parallel circuits and measuring instruments.</p>\n            </a>\n\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/electricity/power-energy/\" class=\"block p-6 bg-white/50 rounded-lg hover:bg-white/60 transition duration-150\">\n              <h5 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Electrical Energy &amp; Power</h5>\n              <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Power calculations and energy considerations in circuits.</p>\n            </a>\n\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/electricity/conduction/\" class=\"block p-6 bg-white/50 rounded-lg hover:bg-white/60 transition duration-150\">\n              <h6 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Conduction in Liquids &amp; Gases</h6>\n              <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Electrolytes, discharge and basic conduction mechanisms.</p>\n            </a>\n\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/electricity/ac-basics/\" class=\"block p-6 bg-white/50 rounded-lg hover:bg-white/60 transition duration-150\">\n              <h7 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">AC Concepts\n              <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">AC vs DC, transformers and basic reactance ideas.</p>\n            </h7></a>\n\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/electricity/electronics/\" class=\"block p-6 bg-white/50 rounded-lg hover:bg-white/60 transition duration-150\">\n              <h8 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Fundamentals of Electronics\n              <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Diodes, transistors and semiconductors at a conceptual level.</p>\n            </h8></a>\n          </div>\n        </div></section>\n\n        <section>\n          <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Why this module</h2>\n          <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\">Start with electrostatics and fields, then move to circuits and electronics; essential for devices and robotics.</p>\n          </div>\n        </section>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-50 to-indigo-100 p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }\n    .content-card {\n      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(16px);\n      backdrop-filter: blur(16px);\n      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);\n      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n      box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\n    }"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}